kind: llman.sdd.delta
ops[5]{op,req_id,title,statement,from,to,name}:
  modify_requirement,tui1,"line-array-differential-render","The TUI MUST render using a self-built differential render engine over a line-array screen representation (previous_lines vs new_lines per-frame diff, writing only changed lines wrapped in synchronized output CSI 2026), driven by crossterm directly for raw mode/events/cursor. The TUI MUST NOT use ratatui (cell-grid Buffer, immediate-mode Widget trait, Viewport::Inline, or insert_before). The engine owns the whole conversation history as a single Vec of styled lines; streaming appends new lines via diff (no irreversible commit). The viewport MUST anchor to the content tail every frame: previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height). Evidence: pi-tui line-array + viewport anchoring (tui.ts:1318-1319 bufferLength = max(height, newLines.length)); the prior ratatui inline-viewport model forced commit-unit = render-unit = paragraph, losing cross-paragraph markdown context (the c396 screenshot root cause).",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui12,"line-array-render-pipeline","The TUI MUST render via a per-frame pipeline: widget tree render(width) produces a flat Vec of StyledLine (the whole conversation), the engine diffs against previous_lines by line equality, picks one of three strategies (first render without clearing, full redraw with clearing, normal diff with line clear + rewrite), wraps writes in synchronized output, positions a virtual IME cursor, and saves state. The hard width invariant MUST fire on both the diff path AND the full-redraw path (an over-wide line is a hard error, not silent wrap). At save-state, previous_viewport_top MUST be set to max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height) centrally in do_render, not in each strategy branch, ensuring the viewport always follows the content tail regardless of the render path taken.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui32,"input-anchored-visual","The TUI input region MUST appear visually at the bottom of the terminal (no floating/gap错觉); the loader status line MUST appear immediately above the input region, also at the visible bottom. When the conversation history exceeds the terminal height, the viewport MUST scroll such that the bottom rows (loader + input) remain in the last visible screen positions, and earlier content scrolls above the viewport. Evidence: c340 §7 leftover #1 noted Viewport::Inline(3) left a perceived gap; pi achieves bottom anchoring via viewport_top = max(0, max(height, lines.length) - height) without any special footer region.",null,null,null
  modify_requirement,tui53,"always-on-status-line","The TUI MUST render a status line between the conversation history and the input panel, occupying exactly one row every frame (idle and streaming). The status line MUST appear at the second-to-last visible row (immediately above the input) regardless of conversation length—the viewport MUST shift upward as content grows to keep the status line + input in the visible bottom. The status line shows a spinner glyph (animated by the existing Tick-driven loader) followed by a single left-aligned activity label: Working while streaming with no tool, Running {tool} while a tool executes, Ready while idle. The status line MUST NOT show a turn count or model name.",null,null,null
  add_requirement,tui84,"viewport-anchoring-single-point","The engine MUST set previous_viewport_top at a single point in do_render (after all strategy branches complete), using the formula max(0, max(terminal_height, total_lines) - terminal_height). Neither diff_render nor full_render MUST modify previous_viewport_top. The anchor formula MUST use max(terminal_height, total_lines) as the working buffer size (pi bufferLength) rather than just total_lines, so short content does not create a transient non-zero viewport offset that causes the footer to drift when content subsequently grows.",null,null,null
op_scenarios[12]{req_id,id,given,when,then}:
  tui1,"viewport-anchors-to-tail","content is 15 rows and terminal height is 10","do_render saves state","previous_viewport_top = 5 (15-10) and scrolling the terminal back shows rows 0-4 in scrollback and rows 5-14 visible"
  tui1,"short-content-anchors-to-zero","content is 3 rows and terminal height is 10","do_render saves state","previous_viewport_top = 0 and all 3 rows plus padding empty rows are visible"
  tui1,"viewport-consistent-across-strategies","content grows from 5 to 15 rows across multiple frames","each frame renders via the appropriate strategy (diff or fullRender)","previous_viewport_top is consistently max(0, max(height, n) - height) regardless of which strategy was used"
  tui12,"viewport-set-in-do-render-only","the engine source is inspected","previous_viewport_top assignment sites are checked","only do_render sets it; diff_render and full_render do not"
  tui32,"footer-visible-when-content-overflows","a ScrollbackTerminal with height=10 renders 15 rows of content (13 history + 1 loader + 1 input)","the engine renders a frame","screen rows 8 and 9 (last two) contain the loader and input lines, and no history line overlaps them"
  tui32,"footer-stays-bottom-during-growth","content grows from 8 rows to 14 rows over 6 frames","each frame is rendered","the loader and input rows are always in the last two screen rows, and the scrollback buffer grows correctly"
  tui53,"status-line-second-to-last","content is 12 rows (10 history + 1 status + 1 input) with terminal height=8","the engine renders a frame","the status line is in screen row 6 and the input line is in screen row 7"
  tui53,"status-line-visible-in-idle","an idle TUI with empty conversation but greeting + loader + input visible","the ScrollbackTerminal frame is inspected","the loader row (second-to-last) shows 'Ready' and the input row (last) shows the prompt cursor"
  tui84,"buffer-length-padding-short-content","content is 2 rows with terminal height=8","do_render sets previous_viewport_top","previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 2) - 8) = 0 (using bufferLength=8, not bufferLength=2)"
  tui84,"buffer-length-normal","content is 12 rows with terminal height=8","do_render sets previous_viewport_top","previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 12) - 8) = 4"
  tui84,"no-viewport-top-modification-in-strategies","the Tui struct fields are inspected after a full render and a diff render","previous_viewport_top is checked","the field is set only by do_render, not mutated inside diff_render or full_render"
  tui84,"viewport-zero-after-clear","content was 15 rows and force_clear triggers a full render with clear of all content","a new frame is rendered with 0 rows","previous_viewport_top = max(0, max(8, 0) - 8) = 0"
